      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The system where creators can choose to have mipmaps for each texture works fine. We don't need to change it to force mipmaps for all textures on all content in the game. \n\nQuest glitter relies on having mipmaps off so the limited screen size causes the high resolution texture to flicker the small dots, creating the glitter effect. With mipmaps forced on the texture just becomes lower quality and you cannot see any of the details. \n\nHigh resolution photos will also not be able to see any details due to forced mipmaps, as the details are lost when the texture resolution is forcefully reduced.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-11-23T05:17:34.923Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Mipmaps are now forced. This breaks quest avatar features like glitter. Please keep the old system of letting creators choose! With MipMap streaming on by default, most avatars will have mipmaps on anyways. No need to force the rest to conform when there are reasons to turn it off.",
